`(7×1.5 + 8×1.5 + 9×1.5 + 8 + 7 + 8×0.5) / 7 = 55.0 / 7 = 7.9`. No caps applied — Discoverability 9 clears the gate, 0 contrast pairs, same-type scan clear, no untagged load-bearing quotes.

### Key observations

**The revision worked on what it targeted.** The first grade (8.1) capped Originality at 7 for cross-draft sameness. Three of the five flagged house moves are genuinely broken now — the TL;DR is declarative sentences instead of the `<li><b>Label:</b>` skeleton that Bill-Burr, Naval-Ravikant and Cara-Delevingne all still run, the corpus-stat sentence is gone, the reader-command imperatives are gone. Cap correctly lifted, Originality to 8.

**It came in lower anyway (7.9, delta 0.2) because Evidence and Writing are weaker than the first grade credited.** Fielder gets three of his own quotes in 3,806 words. The two sources carrying the most weight — the Nolan Q&A (entire cold open, Safdie beat, closing callback) and the Jack Black Q&A (the central pilot's-license motive, one interior beat) — are auto-caption-only and paraphrased throughout. The hook, the ending, and the load-bearing motive all rest on text nobody can quote. The pipeline discloses this honestly; disclosure doesn't remove it.

**The hedging is now the prose's defining feature.** Even after the revision consolidated six hedges into one standing-limits note, the body still carries eight-plus more. Intellectually honest, and it fixes Alex-Warren's "contested typing presented as settled" failing — but the reader is never allowed to sit inside an assertion, and that's what separates this from Matt-Smith.

**Two things stand out as genuinely good:** the central reframe (the persona debate is aimed at the wrong axis — preparation and awkwardness *produce* each other) passes the swap test and no other Fielder profile makes it. And the critic-pressure section is the hardest-faced in the recent batch, including the observation that the harshest line in the premiere is one Fielder commissioned and staged.

**Unusual for this pipeline: the ledgers are accurate.** All 7 H2s exist verbatim, all 5 testimony quotes are in the body attributed and dated. No stale-ledger flag.

**Ledger overclaim worth noting:** the revision notes say two aphoristic section closers were retained under PROTECT. There are five.

The biggest lever to B is already correctly identified in the draft's own notes as *blocked, not declined* — audio-verifying the two Q&As would unlock verbatim Fielder in the cold open and the pilot's-license motive, which moves Evidence on its own.
